{"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/docs.RcloneRC\/documentation\/RcloneRC\/Deadline\/run(seconds:qos:timeoutError:work:)","doc:\/\/docs.RcloneRC\/documentation\/RcloneRC\/Deadline\/run(seconds:qos:work:)"],"title":"Type Methods","generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Methods"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/docs.RcloneRC\/documentation\/RcloneRC\/Deadline","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Deadline","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This exists because the obvious Swift Concurrency approach is wrong in a way that is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"easy to miss. A task group used as a timeout —","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["try await withThrowingTaskGroup(of: T.self) { group in","    group.addTask { try await work() }          \/\/ may block forever","    group.addTask { try await sleep(); throw Timeout() }","    let first = try await group.next()!","    group.cancelAll()                           \/\/ does NOT unblock the first task","    return first","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"— ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"does not time out"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":". A task group will not return until every child task has","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"finished, and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cancelAll()"},{"text":" cannot resume a task suspended on a callback that will","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"never fire, or one blocked in an uninterruptible syscall. The timeout fires, and then","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the group hangs anyway. That was observed here: a probe with a 5-second deadline hung","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"indefinitely against a dead NFS mount.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"grrclone deals in exactly the operations this breaks on — ","type":"text"},{"code":"stat","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" against a wedged NFS","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"mount, ","type":"text"},{"code":"mount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"diskutil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a socket whose listener has died — so the timeout has to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"be real.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The approach below runs the blocking work on a Dispatch thread, which is genuinely"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"abandonable: on timeout the caller stops waiting, and the thread finishes on its own"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and its result is discarded. Nothing structured is waiting on it."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Runs work that cannot be cancelled, and stops waiting for it after a deadline.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/docs.RcloneRC\/documentation\/RcloneRC"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/rclonerc\/deadline"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"title":"Deadline","symbolKind":"enum","roleHeading":"Enumeration","modules":[{"name":"RcloneRC"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Deadline"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Deadline","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:8RcloneRC8DeadlineO"},"references":{"doc://docs.RcloneRC/documentation/RcloneRC/Deadline":{"title":"Deadline","url":"\/documentation\/rclonerc\/deadline","abstract":[{"text":"Runs work that cannot be cancelled, and stops waiting for it after a deadline.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Deadline"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/docs.RcloneRC\/documentation\/RcloneRC\/Deadline","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Deadline"}]},"doc://docs.RcloneRC/documentation/RcloneRC/Deadline/run(seconds:qos:timeoutError:work:)":{"title":"run(seconds:qos:timeoutError:work:)","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/rclonerc\/deadline\/run(seconds:qos:timeouterror:work:)","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Throwing variant, for call sites where a timeout is an error rather than a ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"run"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"T"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"seconds"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"TimeInterval","preciseIdentifier":"c:@T@NSTimeInterval"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"qos"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"DispatchQoS","preciseIdentifier":"s:8Dispatch0A3QoSV"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"QoSClass","preciseIdentifier":"s:8Dispatch0A3QoSV0B6SClassO"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"timeoutError"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"attribute","text":"@autoclosure"},{"kind":"text","text":" () -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Error","preciseIdentifier":"s:s5ErrorP"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"work"},{"kind":"text","text":": () -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"T","preciseIdentifier":"s:8RcloneRC8DeadlineO3run7seconds3qos12timeoutError4workxSd_8Dispatch0J3QoSV0K6SClassOs0H0_pyYbXKxyYbctYaKs8SendableR